Subject: [PATCH 1/2] C21's series, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M37; register row P-849): MAIN'S CHECK OF THE TWELVE OLDER VERDICT LINES OF
 CLASS NEITHER STANDS ON THEIR PAGES AND IN THEIR ROWS

Main checked the 25 older verdict lines marked a selection (M37; P-849 records it): the 13 of class "family named" hold,
and none of the 12 of class "neither" is a selection without its family. This patch carries that check, in main's words:

  - on each of the twelve pages, a dated note after the note of 2026-11-13 that waited for it: eight name the family on
    the page (B44, B125, B266, B1230, B1235, B1298, B1806, B1857), two are deductions (B1228, B1154), two claim no
    selection of their own (B1258, B1406); each with main's words for that arc; the earlier note stays as written;
  - in each of their rows of B1905's older_verdict_lines_classified.json, a field checked_by_main (the day, the row,
    main's class and words); the builder's class stays as read, so the gate's reading and its count are unchanged.

THE LOCK, tests/test_the_twelve_selections_noted.py: each page carries main's check after the note it answers, with
main's class and words, and each row carries it (8, 2 and 2); planted, a page without the check, a row without it, and
a check moved above the note it answers, each reported alone. It names no arc. BEFORE: on the tree before this patch,
the new test fails.

0 of 19.
